					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-225463#post-976943</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-225463/scp-611#post-976943</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 18 Jan 2011 01:53:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Whitewings</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>303995</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Not wanting to dump on an excellent entry, but I feel the need to ask the question I ask for any "weird species" SCP. Why is the Foundation involved? It's just an insect. A weird, health-hazardous insect, to be sure, but why does the Foundation care about this thing? It's not a "threat to normalcy" in any sense I understand, so shouldn't they just leave it to the regular relevant authorities?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
